    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0448" n="352" xml:id="pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894c.111/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-12T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 12—11:08
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Your 10, January 8, 4 p.m. To avoid any possible ambiguity I suggest
                    addressing following note to Japanese Minister: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have the honor to state in amplification of my note[s] of November 2nd
                            and January 5th that the discontinuance after January 15th of my
                            Government’s acquiescence in the application to American citizens of
                            certain passport regulations of the Japanese Government applies equally
                            to the Mukden–Antung railway and the Shantung railway outside of the
                            leased territory.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Does Department concur?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
